# epyc-16: every per-change job — the Nim test shards, pixie, the renderer
# and Playwright shards, backend tests, the deploy E2Es, the ESP32 legs, the
# runtime Docker image, Cloud CI. A wide pull request fans out ~23 of these.
# 16 vCPUs because the jobs are compiles and test runners that use every core
# they get, and the host sat ~90% idle while 4-vCPU slots ran a whole PR
# (2026-11-14). vCPUs are overcommitted on purpose; memory is the budget, and
# 24G is a ceiling for the working set (the guest trims its page cache).
# Also labelled epyc-4: jobs from branches cut before the epyc-16 label ask
# for that, and get the same slot.
CPUS=16
MEMORY=24GiB
DISK=80GiB
LABELS=self-hosted,monster,epyc-16,epyc-4,linux,x64
# Read-only cache except the Nim nimcache archives (test shards, renderer)
# and the ESP32 ccache archives. The workflows save those on pushes to main
# only, but any job here could write them, so nothing a release ships reads
# them (same rule as the old epyc-4 slots' nimcache).
GHA_CACHE_WRITABLE="nimcache ccache"
